# Conventions

## Context

The seeded app (`app/src/types.ts`, `store.ts`, `reducer.ts`, `actions.ts`,
`selectors.ts`, `lib/text.ts`) follows a small, consistent style. Keeping new
code in the same style is what lets the custom store and reducer stay easy to
reason about.

## Rule

- Named exports only — no `export default`.
- No `any` and no `@ts-ignore`/`@ts-expect-error`.
- State updates are always immutable (spread/map/filter), matching the
  pattern in `app/src/reducer.ts` — never `state.tasks.push(...)` or similar.
- File names are kebab-case (e.g. `lib/text.ts`, not `Text.ts`).
- Import local modules with explicit `.js` extensions, matching existing
  imports (e.g. `import type { Action } from "./types.js"`).

## How to verify

1. `grep -rn "export default" app/src` — should find zero matches.
2. `grep -rn "\bany\b\|@ts-ignore\|@ts-expect-error" app/src` — should find
   zero matches.
3. `cd app && npm test` stays green after the change.
